WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.609
Since landing the role of Joi in Blade Runner
2049, actress Ana de Armas has shot into the

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:09.360
spotlight — leaving many sci-fi fans wondering
where they've seen her before.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.180
After starting her acting career in Cuba,
de Armas honed her craft in Spain before making

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.460
the jump to Hollywood and English language
films in 2015.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.680
Here's a look at why Joi from Blade Runner
looks so familiar.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:21.940
Knock Knock

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.140
Ana de Armas' first widely seen English-language
role came in Eli Roth's 2015 erotic horror

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.260
film Knock Knock, in which she terrorizes,
tortures and abuses Keanu Reeves' character.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.740
She told Screen Rant it was a role she enjoyed.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.200
"It was so much fun just going from little
girls to pure psycho."

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.300
De Armas also enjoyed making Reeves uncomfortable
before the cameras started rolling.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.640
"Keanu is shy and feels uncomfortable.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.180
He's not open about talking about his life
in general.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.100
So we were really pushing him to the limit,
playing with him and touching him and whispering

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.830
things to him before the scene.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.100
He was REALLY uncomfortable.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.280
It really worked."

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.580
Exposed

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.870
After ruining Keanu Reeves' life in Knock
Knock, de Armas again teamed up with the soft-spoken

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.180
actor in Gee Malik Linton's 2016 thriller
Exposed.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.090
She told TV Daily that the Reeves taught her
a lot about the craft of acting.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.480
"It's always very easy to be with him on set;
he always wants your work to be better."

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.300
"Keanu is a great partner.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.560
A great actor.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.020
A great producer in this case.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.420
And a great friend."

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:26.360
Reeves also didn't hold back from heaping
praise on de Armas, telling TV Daily "When

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.630
we approached Ana with the script I was like,
please say yes.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.420
It's a great role and she's remarkable.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.020
I only have one scene with her at the end
of the picture, which was great, but I wish

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:35.740
we'd had more."

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.200
War Dogs

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:42.920
de Armas' big 2016 wrapped up with a supporting
role in Todd Phillips' biographical dramedy

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:47.970
War Dogs, in which Jonah Hill and Miles Teller
get caught up in some super shady arms dealing

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:52.909
while exploiting a government initiative allowing
small businesses to win U.S. military contracts

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:54.120
during the Iraq War.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.200
de Armas told Orange Magazine she took the
role in part because she wanted to work with

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:58.720
Phillips.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.340
"Todd is very smart and what I find so remarkable
about him is his ability to put movies together

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.000
that connect so well with audiences.

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:09.200
On the set, he knows what he wants and when
you feel that confidence in your director,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.480
who is the person telling you what he's looking
for, it's amazing."

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:13.840
Overdrive

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.999
It's been overshadowed by Blade Runner 2049,
but you may have seen de Armas in the trailers

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.700
for Overdrive.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.200
The fact that the two films opened on the
same weekend in October, 2017 just about guaranteed

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.440
Overdrive would be overlooked.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.620
But that's not necessarily a bad thing, as
Overdrive has been getting terrible reviews.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.260
The one bright spot, however, is the performance
by de Armas, who The Hollywood Reporter said

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.379
"radiates more kick-ass charisma than her
thankless sidekick role might suggest."

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.880
Hey, you can't win 'em all.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.600
And given how many high-profile features de
Armas has already landed, she doesn't have

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.660
to, because Blade Runner 2049 looks like the
beginning of a beautiful blockbuster career.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:51.940
Thanks for watching!

